<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
  <dict>
    <!-- Entitlements for "Flit Helper.app" ONLY — the bundle Chromium launches
         utility processes from — applied by scripts/sign-utility-helper.mjs
         after electron-builder has signed the bundle. Identical to
         entitlements.mac.inherit.plist plus library validation disabled.

         Why: the Widevine CDM is a dylib DOWNLOADED AT RUNTIME by Chrome's
         component updater (castLabs' Electron does not bundle it). Under the
         hardened runtime, library validation refuses to load a dylib signed by
         another team, so createMediaKeys() fails with "CreateCdmFunc not
         available" even though requestMediaKeySystemAccess() succeeds — that
         only checks the CDM is registered, not that it loads.

         Why this bundle: Electron runs the CDM as a utility process, and
         utility processes launch from the generic "Flit Helper.app" (verified
         from the running process list — network and audio services run from it
         too). Chrome entitles its Helper (Plugin) instead; that bundle is
         legacy PPAPI here and entitling it changed nothing.

         Why not everywhere: this entitlement lets a process load arbitrary
         unsigned libraries. Helper (Renderer).app and Helper (GPU).app have
         their own bundles and deliberately do NOT get it, so the two most
         attack-exposed processes stay fully hardened. The main app does not get
         it either. -->
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
    <true/>
    <!-- Required for Electron (V8 JIT) under the hardened runtime. -->
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
    <true/>
    <!-- Google Meet: microphone + camera. -->
    <key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.device.camera</key>
    <true/>
    <!-- Passkey/security-key sign-in over Bluetooth (caBLE). -->
    <key>com.apple.security.device.bluetooth</key>
    <true/>
  </dict>
</plist>
